{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/70090-here-s-what-bugs-me-about-the-wod","id":70090,"title":"Here's what bugs me about the WoD...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-11T15:40:08-08:00","id":70090,"title":"Here's what bugs me about the WoD...","content":"In another thread,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/69437-classical-greece-as-a-setting-for-vampire-the-masquerade?p=70025#post70025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it is a Masquerade game you are working on but Requiem for Rome and Ancient Mysteries are two modules that bring up some very interesting ideas when it comes to changes in kindred society through different periods or cultures. Check it out if you can.<br /> Nightstalkers, for Hunter the Vigil, discussing hunter groups through the ages and their varied interactions with the undead is also very much worth a look.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sorta seems like a common thing in the WoD now - a sort of &quot;let's steal from nWoD!&quot; (Or vice versa, I suppose, but I don't like nWoD, so I don't care what they do over there.) Anyway. I don't have a problem with any specific suggestion to borrow from elsewhere, per se, so much as the pervasiveness. Is it a good idea? Maybe. Hell, I'll even say probably! But isn't it sometimes just better to say, &quot;That's how the nWoD would do it, sure, but let's go this way.&quot; It just seems like it encourages a sort of creative and intellectual laziness that bothers me.<br /> <br /> Okay rant over. I'd like your thoughts on things, though.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit: I don't mean to call you out specifically, Baaldam - your note just happened to be the one I was reading.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:04:34-08:00","id":70148,"title":"","content":"That comes up on the Exalted boards every now and then, too. Mostly with regard to Attribute choices, since some people just can't accept Appearance standing on its own, or can't think outside of Power/Finesse/Resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T17:50:31-08:00","id":70179,"title":"","content":"The thread was asking about vampires in Classical Greece. If Requiem for Rome or Nightstalkers do have some easy to comprehend history/myth bits within the books: Why is it an issue?<br /> You don't need to borrow everything from a suggested book, like how the supernaturals are in the nwod to your cwod game.<br /> You'll be surprised at the material that sometimes pops up in books, magazines, and other RPG books. For instance, I loved Dragon Magazine for the mythological issue it put out.<br /> <br /> And I know that some people do have a hard time reading regular history books (I'm not one of them).<br /> Then again, this is classical Greece and not Rome: So I would probably find something closer to the era than Requiem for Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:29:21-08:00","id":70580,"title":"","content":"As pointed out, that was the note I was reading - and perhaps not the best example. My concern (also as noted) wasn't with any particular situation, but the trend overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-12T07:50:53-08:00","id":70602,"title":"","content":"I think it's a ridiculous complaint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T11:16:03-08:00","id":72093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/70090-here-s-what-bugs-me-about-the-wod?p=70602#post70602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a ridiculous complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crikey, that's not terribly constructive. What precisely, is ridiculous about it? I am unfamiliar with Requiem, and therefore have no <i>informed </i>opinion one way or the other about the observation made by Big Brother. It may well be a &quot;ridiculous complaint&quot;, Michael, but without elaborating on why you think so, saying so just comes off as terribly, terribly rude (in my humble opinion, of course).<br /> <br /> For my part, I think that a game system (or any iteration thereof) or even very different games are valid source material so long as the story is good, and the themes are consistent. I use rather a lot of Lovecraftian themes and material in my vampire games, for no other material reason than I love it and so do my players. If Requiem has a good thematic or setting idea, I'd be happy to incorporate it into my game. After all, I'm assuming that Requiem would be heavily informed by Masquerade, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/the-concord-of-ashes\" target=\"_blank\">The Concord of Ashes</a>, my Dark Ages Vampire Chronicle","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1790-haligaunt","name":"Haligaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1790_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T12:02:15-08:00","id":72119,"title":"","content":"It's a ridiculous complaint because mining other games for ideas is a valid, if not good, suggestion unless there is something specifically problematic with the game referenced. Suggesting people read FATAL for good ideas is... not going to go over well; and justifiably so because that book has serious issues on almost all levels. Suggesting nWOD sources on a thread that starts with a disclaimer of the OP's utter hatred of the nWOD and absolute lack of interest in it is rude.<br /> <br /> The idea that the nWOD gets suggested at lot as something to mine for ideas for cWOD games is inherently problematic? That's pretty much ridiculous. They're related systems, with related themes, and the nWOD has gotten to explore a few concepts that the cWOD didn't. There is no rational reason to have a problem with cWOD threads being about, or including, mining the nWOD for ideas. Doing shit just because it isn't the way the nWOD does it when we're talking about developing content for our own personal game-play experiences is flat out bad advice. Maybe the nWOD was is good for what you want, maybe it isn't. Going the other way on general principle means you are putting dislike of the nWOD over what might be best for your game. Which is fine if that's a personal preference, but it is ridiculous to consider as a larger scale problem.<br /> <br /> VtR, for example, has a supplement that has some pretty big support for being a great supplement even for non-WOD games. <i>Damnation City</i> is seen by a chunk of people as a wonderful city building source book, even after you cut out the minimal Vampire specific parts of it. It is only game-line specific book I would flat out suggest to anyone running the nWOD because the content is just that applicable if you want a book's help on developing a city for your game.<br /> <br /> And to address your last question:<br /> <br /> Requiem is heavily informed by Masquerade. Though that goes in a few directions (and has changed a bit in expression over the past decade). Requiem has aspects that are clearly hold overs that the designers thought were worth maintaining from Masquerade, and things that were rather blatantly changed because of how they worked in Masquerade in application. On top of new ideas that came from other sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-14T21:15:06-08:00","id":72454,"title":"","content":"Now that is a beautiful and informative answer, Cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/the-concord-of-ashes\" target=\"_blank\">The Concord of Ashes</a>, my Dark Ages Vampire Chronicle","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1790-haligaunt","name":"Haligaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1790_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T00:54:51-08:00","id":72508,"title":"","content":"@ Heavy Arms<br /> <br /> A really excellent response to the topic, agree 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-15T12:45:56-08:00","id":72777,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest issue isn't that you borrow from other games - I do that a lot, too, after all. My problem is that with VtR you're taking VtM, mangling it, increasing the price, then re-selling it. I feel like if they wanted to go a different route, they should have - y'know - gone a different route. Instead, I feel like they're taking my money, and saying, &quot;But so's we don't lose the VtM fans, let's throw in some similar-sounding words.&quot; (However, I'm getting off topic.)<br /> <br /> Heavy, while I disagree in part, I appreciate how thought through your response was, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T01:26:51-08:00","id":73089,"title":"","content":"They are two very similar games about vampires thriving in the modern day through a secret neo-feudal society, they both have huge amounts of material written for them, much of it really good. Borrowing from wither to the other feels very natural, they kind of blend together like sides of a coin. Its a bit like saying that you should not recommend any material for one DnD world while playing in another, its just absurd.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/70090-here-s-what-bugs-me-about-the-wod?p=72777#post72777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest issue isn't that you borrow from other games - I do that a lot, too, after all. My problem is that with VtR you're taking VtM, mangling it, increasing the price, then re-selling it. I feel like if they wanted to go a different route, they should have - y'know - gone a different route. Instead, I feel like they're taking my money, and saying, &quot;But so's we don't lose the VtM fans, let's throw in some similar-sounding words.&quot; (However, I'm getting off topic.)<br /> <br /> Heavy, while I disagree in part, I appreciate how thought through your response was, thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, now you are just basing it on your own misunderstandings and I would assume unfamiliarity with the material. Have you looked at Requiem For Rome and Ancient Mysteries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T02:36:12-08:00","id":73109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Big Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/70090-here-s-what-bugs-me-about-the-wod?p=72777#post72777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is that with VtR you're taking VtM, mangling it, increasing the price, then re-selling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's how you feel about VtR, then that's how you feel about VtR. But that's also your personal opinion. It doesn't really extend well towards you initial complaint that there is a problem with a &quot;trend&quot; of mining the nWOD for cWOD games.<br /> <br /> If/when you start threads for ideas on inspiration for stuff that VtM doesn't cover you should feel free to express your distaste for VtR and disinterest in suggestions from VtR. People should respect that. But not everyone shares your views on VtR. Some people like it better. Some people don't care. Some people like both equally for different reasons (esp. more recent VtR culminating with Blood &amp; Smoke; as it has taken VtR a big leap forward in stepping out from behind VtM's shadow at least on a design level). Some people haven't read it and don't know if they like it or not. For anyone that doesn't have a negative opinion about VtR, suggestions to mine from it aren't problematic. So the concept of there being a problematic trend doesn't materialize.<br /> <br /> Also, because this one point tends to irk me a bit: VtR's increased selling price is basic inflation. It was a $5 increase in price for a book of the same length, size, and comparable cost factors (well, actually, VtR has slightly higher base cost factors because isn't a purely B&amp;W interior whether you consider the inclusion of red ink in the first VtR book a worthy artistic choice is pretty subjective). As a comparison, I pulled a 2000 softcover printing of a novel in a series. It cost $7. A 2004 novel in the same series that was the same length was $8 for the paperback.<br /> <br /> Most people don't realize that the Revised era cWOD books were actually priced well below what they realistically should have been given increased costs on the production end of things. WW chose to keep the costs closer to 2e costs to avoid sticker shock even as production costs went up. When the nWOD came out, they upped the costs to better match the production costs of the day; and like most RPG books charge way less than comparable books in less niche (or other factors like text book price controls) markets. It was really that simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heavy, while I disagree in part, I appreciate how thought through your response was, thank you. </div> </div> </div>Thanks for taking the time to give my dissent a fair read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-16-2014, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-16T07:16:18-08:00","id":73169,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Edition warring is against the forum rules. This is starting to step over the line, so I'm locking the thread. I may reopen it later once everyone's had some time to think about what's been said.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}